// examples/markdown-showcase/Jenkinsfile
//
// Self-contained demo of the interactive-ci Markdown rendering, exercising the constructs that the
// Interactive View viewer (and the askInteractive modal context panel) render — with emphasis on the
// GitHub-Flavored Markdown extensions this plugin enables: TABLES, STRIKETHROUGH and AUTOLINKS.
//
// How to run:
//   1. Create a Pipeline job and paste this file in (or commit it as a Jenkinsfile and point the job at it).
//   2. Run it. It needs an agent with a workspace ("agent any") because interactiveView snapshots a file
//      from the build's workspace.
//   3. Open the build's "Interactive View" sidebar link (or the notification bell) to see the rendered
//      Markdown. Stages 2 and 3 BLOCK on a human decision by design (a review gate / an approval).
//
// The full "every construct" reference lives next to this file in markdown-showcase.md; point
// `interactiveView(file: ...)` at it after an SCM checkout if you want the exhaustive version.

pipeline {
    agent any
    options {
        timestamps()
    }
    stages {

        stage('Write showcase markdown') {
            steps {
                // A dollar-slashy string ($/ ... /$) so backslashes, pipes and backticks are all literal.
                writeFile file: 'markdown-showcase.md', text: $/# Markdown rendering demo

## 1. Emphasis
**bold**, _italic_, ***bold italic***, ~~strikethrough~~ and `inline code`.

## 2. Table with column alignment (:-- left, :-: center, --: right)
| Left        | Center | Right |
|:------------|:------:|------:|
| a           | b      | 1     |
| longer cell | mid    | 1000  |
| x           | y      | 42    |

## 3. Table with inline formatting inside cells
| Feature       | Example                          | Status              |
|---------------|----------------------------------|---------------------|
| bold + code   | **`retryCount`** must be `>= 0`  | ~~deprecated~~ **active** |
| link in cell  | see [the docs](https://www.jenkins.io/) | OK           |
| escaped pipe  | `a \| b` renders literally       | OK                  |

## 4. Lists
- unordered
  - nested
    - deeper
1. ordered
2. second
   1. sub-item

## 5. Blockquote
> A quote with **bold** and `code`.
> > A nested quote.

## 6. Autolinks
Bare URL: https://plugins.jenkins.io/interactive-ci/ and e-mail dev@example.com

## 7. Fenced code block (shown as escaped source)
```java
public String render(String md) {
    return RENDERER.render(PARSER.parse(md));
}
```

## 8. Inline HTML is escaped, never executed
<script>alert('xss')</script> and an entity: &copy; 2026, 5 &lt; 10.
/$
                echo 'Wrote markdown-showcase.md'
            }
        }

        stage('Publish as an informational viewer (non-blocking)') {
            steps {
                script {
                    // mode:'info' is a read-only, still-commentable viewer with no approve/reject buttons.
                    def id = interactiveView(
                        file: 'markdown-showcase.md',
                        reportName: 'Markdown showcase',
                        title: 'Markdown rendering showcase (info)',
                        mode: 'info',
                        notify: true,
                        commentable: true,
                        editable: true
                    )
                    echo "Published informational review: ${id}"
                }
            }
        }

        stage('Blocking review gate (waits for a human decision)') {
            steps {
                script {
                    // wait:true pauses the pipeline until a reviewer approves / rejects / requests changes.
                    def r = interactiveView(
                        file: 'markdown-showcase.md',
                        reportName: 'Markdown showcase',
                        title: 'Markdown rendering showcase (review + wait)',
                        mode: 'review',
                        wait: true,
                        slaMinutes: 60,
                        commentable: true,
                        editable: true
                    )
                    echo "Decision: ${r.status} by ${r.decidedBy}"
                    if (r.status == 'CHANGES_REQUESTED') {
                        // On "Request changes" the reviewer's inline comments come back for a regenerate loop.
                        r.comments.each { c -> echo "line ${c.line}: ${c.body}" }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        stage('askInteractive with a table in the modal context') {
            steps {
                script {
                    // The modal's context panel renders the same Markdown pipeline, so tables/strikethrough/
                    // autolinks now render there too.
                    def ans = askInteractive(
                        prompt: 'Approve the configuration matrix below?',
                        contextMarkdown: $/| Setting     | Value        |
|-------------|--------------|
| replicas    | **3**        |
| ~~debug~~   | disabled     |

See https://www.jenkins.io/ for details./$,
                        choices: [[id: 'approve', label: 'Approve'], [id: 'reject', label: 'Reject']],
                        allowFreeText: true,
                        slaMinutes: 60
                    )
                    echo "askInteractive answer: ${ans}"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
